# Investigation 1 — Review Failed Authentication Attempts

## Purpose

Review all failed SSH authentication attempts to understand the nature of the activity.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
| order by TimeGenerated asc
```

### Why It Matters

This provides investigators with the initial evidence needed to understand the authentication failures and identify attack patterns.

---

# Investigation 2 — Investigate a Suspicious Source IP

## Purpose

Review all events associated with a specific source IP address.

### Query

```kusto
let SuspiciousIP = "203.0.113.77";

MeridianLogs_CL
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)",1,RawData)
| where SourceIP == SuspiciousIP
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
| order by TimeGenerated asc
```

### Why It Matters

Reviewing all activity from a single IP address helps determine whether the behavior is isolated or part of a larger attack.

---

# Investigation 3 — Build an Event Timeline

## Purpose

Create a chronological timeline of authentication activity.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
| order by TimeGenerated asc
```

### Why It Matters

Event timelines allow analysts to reconstruct attacker activity and understand the sequence of events leading to an alert.

---

# Investigation 4 — Identify Targeted Systems

## Purpose

Determine which systems experienced the highest volume of authentication events.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| summarize TotalEvents = count() by Computer
| order by TotalEvents desc
```

### Example Output

| Computer | Total Events |
|----------|-------------:|
| server01 | 175 |
| server02 | 116 |

### Why It Matters

Identifying frequently targeted systems helps prioritize investigative efforts and assess business impact.

---

# Investigation 5 — Search for Successful Authentication

## Purpose

Determine whether repeated failed login attempts were eventually followed by a successful authentication.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Accepted password"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
```

### Why It Matters

A successful login after numerous failed attempts may indicate that an attacker successfully obtained valid credentials.

